# Open items live in the repo

Chat is fleeting. Anything the user would need after this session goes
in one of three places, in the same turn you notice it:

- **Code** — small and in scope: do it.
- **The doc being tracked** — a handoff or design doc in `docs/` for
  this work: add a `- [ ]` box under the owning section (Worker / PWA /
  Cab / Helm / crane) saying what, why, and where the fix goes. Refresh
  the doc's "Open" summary line if it has one. Tick `[x]` with a short
  note when done.
- **The todo list** — this-session work: add a todo.

This covers a gap you noticed on a sibling surface (PWA vs Cab vs Helm),
something you chose not to do, a limitation of the approach you took, a
test you did not write, a doc that now describes the wrong behaviour.

Do not end a turn with "one note…", "not done here…", or "say the word
if you want it" as the only record. If it is worth a sentence in chat,
it is worth a box in the doc.

When a change alters behaviour a doc describes (`docs/frontends.md`,
`docs/voice.md`, a handoff doc), update that doc in the same change.

Before the final summary, reread it: every follow-up named there is
already in a doc or the todo list, and the summary says where.

```text
❌ BAD — chat only
  One note for the PWA, not done here: it has no draft TTL. Say the word.

✅ GOOD — docs/draft_stream_handoff.md, PWA section, same turn
  - [ ] **Draft TTL.** No mouth-local expiry; a crane that hangs without
        closing leaves the bubble until the next `reply`. Cab has 60 s.
        Mirror it in `PhoneShell`; test with fake timers.
  (summary: "PWA draft TTL is open — boxed in draft_stream_handoff.md")
```
